Lane A owns the shared synth. Do not apply this from lane D.

Viridian Gym spinners play SFX_ARROW_TILES when the spin starts
(engine/overworld/spinners.asm). Route 22 Gate plays SFX_DENIED between the
two refusal lines. Route 23 plays it after the refusal line and before the
step down. The notes are audio1:SFX_Arrow_Tiles_1 and audio1:SFX_Denied_1
from pret/pokered af519899. KantoSynth.sfx asserts on an unknown name, and
these two scores are not in the generated table. The endgame plans already
ask for arrow_tiles and denied. Playback is wrapped in pcall until this lands.

tools/tests/test_lane_d_endgame.py marks
test_arrow_and_denied_scores_are_in_the_synth as an expected failure.

